1
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:09,759
["How To Say Goodbye" playing]

2
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:13,805
♪ Thought this was what you wanted ♪

3
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:17,267
♪ Oh oh oh oh oh oh oh ♪

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:21,271
♪ Now looking back down on us ♪

5
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:24,524
♪ Oh oh oh oh oh oh oh ♪

6
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:28,069
♪ You keep pulling me underneath ♪

7
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:30,739
♪ Why couldn't we learn to leave ♪

8
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,824
♪ Don't you think that it's time ♪

9
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,784
♪ But we still don't know ♪

10
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,245
♪ Still don't know… ♪

11
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:38,997
[Chrishell] I'm so glad I'm here.

12
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:44,002
-[Shonda] You wanna get in the car?
-[Chrishell] It's freezing here.

13
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:45,336
[Shonda] I'm sorry.

14
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,466
Sorry, I only dressed for L.A. weather.

15
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:53,511
It's just a real relief to be with Shonda

16
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:55,847
because, you know, she's my big sister

17
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,557
and at this point in time,

18
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,101
I need someone to take care of me
for a second.

19
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,311
Just kind of regroup.

20
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:03,855
And this is exactly where I know
I need to be.

21
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,734
[Shonda] So how was your flight?

22
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:10,320
The flight was actually good.
Like, I didn't--

23
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:11,529
So no issues?

24
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,948
I feel like I was recognized a few times,

25
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,076
but no one, like, came over
or asked me questions

26
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,202
or said anything so…

27
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:18,661
We were worried about that.

28
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:21,414
I still think I'm in shock to be honest.

29
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:23,416
Well, I think we're all in shock.

30
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,461
I'm so mad.

31
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,547
I say that, and then I wanna cry. Sorry.

32
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:31,883
[Chrishell gasps] I don't know
what I'm feeling right now.

33
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:33,718
[Shonda] I think that's okay.

34
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:37,472
I think that it's gonna take a few days
for you to process what happened.

35
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:41,726
I just can't believe everyone's
finding out when I'm finding out.

36
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:45,730
I had literally no time to--

37
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:50,777
The people that were in our wedding
found out through TMZ.

38
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:53,655
You know what I mean?
That's so disrespectful.

39
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:57,283
And he couldn't have given me a heads-up?
He couldn't have…

40
00:02:00,161 --> 00:02:04,624
I just--
I'll never, ever be able to comprehend how

41
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:08,086
this is how someone would choose
to handle something like this…

42
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:09,921
-[Shonda] No.
-…in the public eye.

43
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:12,882
[Chrishell] Like, you go to therapy
and you talk about it,

44
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:17,762
or you talk about it with family members
and you have a plan in place.

45
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:20,014
Like, this is not--
You don't just, like…

46
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:22,767
-make a decision and then text someone.
-[Shonda] Yeah.

47
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,813
[scoffs] I can't even believe
these words are coming out of my mouth.

48
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:30,233
I'm still in shock. That doesn't even
sound like real life what I just said.

49
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,693
That is insanity.

50
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:34,404
[Shonda] There needs to be
a proper ending. Like a proper way

51
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,447
to speak to somebody and communicate.

52
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:40,410
Just the respect that you owe that person
that you've spent so much time with.

53
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:43,329
-I mean, we were together for six years.
-[Shonda] Right.

54
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:46,457
And then you just… throw-- [scoffs]

55
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:49,085
I'm--

56
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:55,425
I'm… I don't know…  I need to, like…

57
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,511
exhale and, like… [sighs]

58
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:08,021
Well, that's what you're here
to do. I'm gonna personally pamper you.

59
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,522
I'm gonna take care of you.

60
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:13,359
Thank you. That sounds wonderful.

61
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,825
♪ I'm a warrior ♪

62
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,495
♪ I'm a warrior ♪

63
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:29,417
♪ Never gonna hold me down ♪

64
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:34,756
♪ Solid as a rock
I'm ready for a challenge ♪

65
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:38,134
♪ Hard as you can hit
Can't knock me off my balance ♪

66
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:47,185
[Amanza] I have to find a buyer
for the Stanley house.

67
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,604
We just did
a 100,000 dollar price reduction.

68
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:52,899
So, hoping this is the move
that we need to sell.

69
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:56,694
♪ I'm gonna stand up
I'm a warrior… ♪

70
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,071
[knocking]

71
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:00,573
-Hello, Amanza?
-[Amanza] Hi.

72
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:01,866
[man] Hey. How's it going?

73
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,952
-I'm well, thank you. How are you?
-[man] Good.

74
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:06,871
[Amanza] Good to see you.
-Good to see you. Beautiful home.

75
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,623
Yeah, it's really nice.

76
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:11,000
-[Amanza] Hopefully-- yeah, take it.
-[Patrick] Thank you.

77
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:13,419
[Amanza] I'm excited
you have a possible buyer.

78
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,880
I'm excited that you have a possible home
for my client.

79
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:18,299
I've been looking for him
for about two years.

80
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:19,425
Wow.

81
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:22,720
I literally feel like I've been trying
to sell this house for, like, two years.

82
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,555
I got wrinkles. I'm getting old.

83
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,891
But Patrick's client is a designer,

84
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,059
so now it makes sense

85
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:30,812
because we designers
can be a little bit picky.

86
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:33,481
I need something with high ceilings, 

87
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:35,984
nice open space, beautiful backyard, so…

88
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,568
Well, I mean, this is amazing.

89
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,658
-[Patrick] Wow. It's gorgeous.
-[Amanza] It's like an oasis.

90
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:45,535
-Yeah. It's beautiful.
-[Amanza] It's so quiet,

91
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:48,496
-just the sound of the waterfall.
-[Patrick] It doesn't feel like the city.

92
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:49,622
I wanna sell this thing,

93
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,791
-but I'll miss doing open houses.
-[Patrick] I'm sure.

94
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:54,377
[laughs] Just pretended it was my house
for a while. So…

95
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:58,089
-What are we looking at square footage?
-It's about 2,476. 

96
00:04:58,172 --> 00:04:59,966
-What's he looking for?
-In that general range.

97
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:01,926
A few bedrooms, you know,
he likes to entertain.

98
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,762
Is your client into cooking at all?
Because this kitchen's amazing.

99
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:05,722
Definitely.

100
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,770
Patrick's client
actually lives in New York,

101
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:14,939
but because they've worked together
for so long,

102
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,691
he knows exactly what he wants.

103
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:20,320
What's cool also about this house,
is they kept its original charm,

104
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:23,823
but everything's just updated.
So it's still got that character.

105
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:25,950
I love the nice, updated,
brand-new appliances,

106
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:28,619
and with the breakfast nook
and the large window looking out.

107
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,288
[Amanza] It's really charming.

108
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,831
There's a fireplace and…

109
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:34,083
[Patrick] Nice. Love the windows.
Beautiful.

110
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:37,253
-[Amanza] The touches of stained glass--
-[Patrick] Yeah, it's gorgeous.

111
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:40,506
-[Amanza] It's pretty cool.
-[Patrick] What's the asking price again?

112
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,632
Two three nine nine.

113
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:46,471
The seller is very motivated,
and we've had a lot of action,

114
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:48,056
but just no firm offers yet.

115
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:52,060
Not only is the seller motivated,
I'm motivated to sell this place.

116
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:54,479
My baby's gotta eat, I need new hair,

117
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,773
and I think Patrick's client
might be the one.

118
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:00,026
I gotta run to another appointment.
Let me go talk to him,

119
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:01,069
and I'll let you know.

120
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:01,986
[Amanza] Okay.

121
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:06,991
I think that went well. I just really hope
that they come back with an offer,

122
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:10,203
because I don't wanna go to Jason
with any more bad news.

123
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:12,872
It's time to bring him something positive.

124
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,543
[sighs]

125
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:22,382
♪ The future is calling ♪

126
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:26,677
♪ I'm taking it all in ♪

127
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:29,013
[Heather] I have to tell you
what Tarek did for me.

128
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:32,850
It's, like, sentimental, but my parents,
they-- we live in the mountains,

129
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:36,687
and that's where I grew up, and the house
next door became, like, for sale.

130
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:40,483
It's like a little cabin. So he bought me
a house. He bought me the cabin, yeah.

131
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:42,568
[Davina] I love that. That's very sweet.

132
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:47,907
-[Christine] I don't understand, a cabin?
-A little, itty-bitty mountain cabin. 

133
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:51,536
Right next door to my parents, and then
my grandpa's on the other side.

134
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:53,788
I know that you can have cabin fever.

135
00:06:53,871 --> 00:06:56,833
I know that there's, like,
horror movies about living in cabins.

136
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:59,919
[laughs] What the fuck is a cabin?
I really don't know.

137
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:01,838
Are you excited about your wedding?

138
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:05,258
-Yeah, I'm really excited.
-So is everyone in the office invited?

139
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:07,885
-Is everyone coming?
-Yeah. I mean, unlike certain people,

140
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:12,014
-I invite everyone. I'm very inclusive.
-[Davina] I know what that feels like.

141
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:14,183
[Christine] I want everyone to come.

142
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:17,019
The only person
I haven't heard back from is Chrishell.

143
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,480
I really want to be excited
for my wedding but, obviously,

144
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:23,526
it's overshadowed by Chrishell's divorce.
It's just hard with her and I.

145
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:26,696
I don't know if I should reach out to her
and ask if she's coming

146
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:28,406
or just assume that she's coming.

147
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:31,909
I feel like,
given our very minimal friendship,

148
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,454
I'm just gonna let her come to me,

149
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,539
and hopefully she'll come.

150
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:38,666
It's nice that you invited her though,
'cause like--

151
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:41,210
-[Christine] Of course.
-…unlike what I went through with Mary.

152
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:43,671
You know, I would love to know
that for Chrishell--

153
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:46,549
-At least she's wanted.
-If it were me, like,

154
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:49,427
I would just want to get out of the house,
be around friends.

155
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:52,138
You know, this is no backyard wedding.
I mean, this is an event.

156
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:55,641
So if anything would help Chrishell
take her mind off this, it's this event.

157
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:59,687
Come to my wedding, dance, drink,
have a fucking steak, a cocktail shrimp,

158
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:01,439
whatever, you know? Have a good time.

159
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,900
I don't know what I would do.
I'd probably wanna go spend time

160
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:07,987
with my family while things settle down,
and the media goes away and then--

161
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,072
Because she's so famous. 

162
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,367
All the cameras were just like…
all over her.

163
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:15,870
[Davina] The Oscars'll probably be on hold
till she comes back.

164
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,496
[Christine laughs] Yeah, exactly.

165
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,291
How do they know where you are, though?
[beeping]

166
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:24,462
I'm on the corner of… [laughs]

167
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,756
Her whole life is here,
but it was with Justin.

168
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:27,924
-So…
-Yeah, of course. 

169
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:30,051
And they probably have a lot
of mutual friends too,

170
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:32,094
so it's hard. She's gonna have
to probably,

171
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:34,180
maybe be a little nicer to me,

172
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:36,474
rebuild up, you know, the other friends.

173
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:39,393
I'm not gonna, like, coexist
and block people out of my life.

174
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:42,063
-I really hope she comes.
-Well, I'm excited.

175
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:44,607
-I am too, it's gonna be fabulous.
-You're wearing black, right?

176
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,108
-I'll wear black--
-[Davina] Cool.

177
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,945
-It's, like, a very sparkly--
-[Davina] Very festive.

178
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:52,490
-…poofy.
-With a veil? Long train and veil?

179
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:55,243
You know what? I think
I'm just gonna pretend it's my wedding!

180
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:56,619
[all laugh]

181
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:58,287
Alright, I'm here guys!

182
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:02,792
[Heather sings the Wedding March]

183
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:04,794
-[Christine] She's so funny.
-[Davina] Can't wait.

184
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:08,214
It'll be my night. Might even grab Tarek
and bring him up with me.

185
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:09,924
-[Davina] It's so good.
-I love it.

186
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,050
[upbeat pop playing]

187
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:18,182
So cute.

188
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:20,351
[Shonda] After you.

189
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:24,522
My older sister Shonda lives in St. Louis
with her husband and three kids.

190
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:27,650
And she's an aesthetician
who owns the spa.

191
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:29,151
So I'm really lucky

192
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,737
that I'm getting taken care of
by the very best.

193
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,870
[Chrishell sighs] That's so nice.

194
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:43,416
I am excited to get a facial
from the master.

195
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:46,002
-Oh, what's that?
-[Shonda] This is your mask.

196
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:49,046
-[Chrishell] Do I look crazy right now?
-No, you look beautiful.

197
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,299
-[Chrishell] You have to say that.
-You look beautiful.

198
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:53,884
It's hard not to feel worthless
in this moment.

199
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:56,304
It's hard not to feel like
everyone's laughing at you.

200
00:09:56,387 --> 00:10:00,391
So it's just such a relief
to be with my family and to see Shonda.

201
00:10:00,474 --> 00:10:04,603
And I just really needed this,
and it's perfect.

202
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,688
Some wine.

203
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:07,440
Thank you.

204
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:10,443
Never had a facial like this,
but… cheers.

205
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:13,863
I'm sorry it's under these circumstances.

206
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:18,284
Like, what's going on?
I still don't really understand, like--

207
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:21,245
-Did you feel there was a sign?
-A sign?

208
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:25,166
I don't really know that there's a sign
that somebody's going to file for divorce

209
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:27,752
with no face-to-face conversation. 

210
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:30,671
When I got home that night,
everything was fine.

211
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:34,258
But, we got into an argument.
When I look back on it…

212
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,594
part of me thinks…

213
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:39,221
he had made a decision…

214
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:41,140
and…

215
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:47,521
I wasn't given a say in this. 

216
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:50,941
-[Shonda] Sweetie.
-Sorry. [gasping]

217
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:55,988
I just-- Part of me can't wrap my brain
around the fact that…

218
00:10:57,656 --> 00:11:04,121
he would make such a hasty decision
without sitting me down and talking to me.

219
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:08,250
But then the other part of me
uses that to realize,

220
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,835
like, he had made a decision.

221
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:13,297
There was--
He didn't want to be talked out of it.

222
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:16,092
It has to have--
be two people that want to be married.

223
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:19,095
Like, you can't just have one person. 
[sniffles]

224
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,682
[sniffles] And I just feel like
it was just me…

225
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:25,685
[gasps] fighting for something that…

226
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:28,729
was a lost cause because he didn't…

227
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:31,982
care enough to even sit me down
and tell me.

228
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:36,654
I get it.
Like, that's a lot to change in your life,

229
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:40,241
all that money and fame
and all that stuff, but…

230
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,077
it shouldn't change how you treat people.

231
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,162
I know, baby.

232
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:48,582
-I'm sorry. [laughs]
-[Shonda] No, this has,

233
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:52,336
I think, been hard for everybody.
You have been his biggest supporter,

234
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,964
and you were there
for him through everything.

235
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:59,343
-A lot has changed with him.
-I would've done anything for him. [sighs]

236
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,012
I think there's nothing you could've done.

237
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:06,517
Yeah, 'cause you work so hard to, like,
make choices to, like, prop someone up

238
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,853
and support their life and what they want,

239
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:12,773
and now, all of a sudden, I'm like,
"Wait a minute… What do I want?"

240
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:14,900
You've been through so much.

241
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,987
You have so much strength,
and you have done so much already.

242
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:21,449
-You don't need anybody. Except us.
-[repeating] I need you.

243
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:24,910
[Chrishell] To be honest,
when I look at what's going on,

244
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,455
it doesn't really feel like my life.

245
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:31,542
It feels so surreal. It feels like this is
something that happens to other people.

246
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:34,086
This isn't something
that actually happens to you.

247
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,130
And so, I just kind of feel like

248
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:38,507
I'm putting one foot
in front of the other,

249
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:42,178
and just trying to keep moving
to the right place,

250
00:12:42,261 --> 00:12:45,055
which is at this point,
you know, my family.

251
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:47,850
And, hopefully,
I'll wake up from this nightmare.

252
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:50,603
-[Chrishell] I love you so much.
-[Shonda] I love you.

253
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:54,398
You make me feel like I can--

254
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,276
you might be right,
just because I have you.

255
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,403
[Chrishell] I don't want to flash you.

256
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:03,324
Like, we're having a sentimental moment,
then my boob pops out.

257
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:05,743
[both laugh]

258
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:09,205
Although they are pretty nice,
I paid a lot of money for them.

259
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:11,624
["Get Down" playing]

260
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:19,924
♪ Call me a renegade
I'm on a moving train ♪

261
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:23,886
♪ You say go left , I'm going right
Better get out of the way ♪

262
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:27,264
[repeating] ♪ Oh oh ♪

263
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:33,813
♪ You can't slow me down ♪

264
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:36,774
♪ Watch me, watch me now ♪

265
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:42,279
♪ Full speed ahead 
I'm on the edge, I'm burning rubber ♪

266
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:44,990
♪ Nothing's gonna low me down ♪

267
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,078
[Mary] Today I'm showing Alpine,

268
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,247
which is the listing
that Brett brought me onto.

269
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,623
It's in a different area.

270
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:54,834
I'm used to showing homes
in the Hollywood Hills,

271
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,377
and this is in Beverly Hills.

272
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:00,047
So I'm super excited
to be showing in a different area,

273
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:03,050
and these are bigger homes,
which means bigger clients.

274
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,553
-Hey, Mary.
-[Mary] Well, hello, how are you?

275
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:07,888
-Doing good. Nice to see you.
-Nice to see you. 

276
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:11,433
I'm glad that you were able to come.
I know you've been working with Jason

277
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,686
for a while,
and we just listed this property.

278
00:14:13,769 --> 00:14:15,646
I thought it would be
kind of a good fit for you.

279
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:19,233
-[Oliver] Looks better than the pictures.
-Well, that's good,

280
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:21,318
'cause we normally do
really, really great pictures.

281
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:24,113
So my client, Oliver,
he has a very unique vision,

282
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:26,448
and he's not afraid
to tell me what that is.

283
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:30,411
So it will be interesting to find out
if he likes Alpine.

284
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:34,748
[Mary] It's about 6,400 square feet
in the flats of Beverly Hills.

285
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:38,252
♪ Like what you see
You won't believe ♪

286
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:40,170
♪ Got what you need ♪

287
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:43,173
We just listed it
at nine million, four-nine-five.

288
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:46,468
Six bedrooms, six baths,
beautiful pool in the back.

289
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:50,306
You've got the formal dining here,
a formal living here.

290
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:53,559
Nice open little living space here,

291
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:55,144
you can see down below.

292
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:58,939
The master is a room that,
I think, has so much potential.

293
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,984
High ceilings, so bright and open.

294
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:05,613
And then, I think the kitchen
is a really great selling point.

295
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:10,951
There's even an indoor water feature,
basically a pond by the staircase.

296
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:14,038
[Oliver] Interesting.
How did a fireplace end up in the pond?

297
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:17,708
-[Mary] I don't know. [laughs]
-[Oliver] Guess the fish gotta stay warm.

298
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:19,627
-[Oliver] Where next?
-[Mary] Backyard.

299
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,632
[Mary] Nice flat lot,
cool cabana over there, nice-sized pool.

300
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:25,841
[Oliver] Look at the pool.

301
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:29,261
It's the weirdest shaped pool I've ever
seen. The current owners built this house?

302
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:32,056
So the current owners
did build this house.

303
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:34,642
This must be like a Feng Shui,
zen design.

304
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:37,311
-[Mary] Yeah.
-I don't think I've seen a house like it.

305
00:15:37,394 --> 00:15:40,481
I like this cabana idea,
but I like having a pool to the side

306
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:42,274
-rather dead-on.
-[Mary] Right.

307
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:45,903
It's cool you can see the yard over here,
but I'd want to see a little bit more.

308
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:49,073
Open up these doors, pulling out
all the cabinets all the way down,

309
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:52,076
opening up the sliding doors here as well.
The waves just don't work.

310
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:55,913
Take away the rounder features. This room
could totally be taken out as well.

311
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:58,582
The staircase would look really cool
in all glass.

312
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,876
I could see someone living in this house,
it's beautiful.

313
00:16:00,959 --> 00:16:03,671
But, for me, in order to create value,

314
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:06,507
I'd have to make it
geared towards today's design standards.

315
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:08,217
Bring everything to a next level.

316
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:11,345
Oliver definitely keeps me on my toes.
I've gotta keep up.

317
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:13,847
I'm wondering
if other Beverly Hills clients 

318
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,766
are like this as well. I guess we'll see.

319
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:18,644
-[Mary] I'm glad I brought you in here.
-[Oliver] Yeah. It's cool.

320
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:22,064
["Shake, Shake, Shake" playing]
♪ 'Cause I'm on top, and I won't stop ♪

321
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:25,234
♪ Can you feel
The whole earth start to quake ♪

322
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:28,362
♪ Can you feel it
Shake shake shake shake ♪

323
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:29,279
♪ Shake shake ♪

324
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:32,866
♪ I'mma keep it going
Till the ceiling's raised ♪

325
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:36,120
[Amanza] There's chicken noodle soup,
Marla, in the refrigerator

326
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:37,454
in a Pink Dot bag.

327
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,916
-[Marla] Okay.
-Buddy, you can't even hold the phone up?

328
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,210
-[Braker] Mama?
-[Marla] Isn't he cute?

329
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:46,839
He's the cutest.
Okay. Bye-bye, I gotta go, okay? Love you.

330
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,049
[Amanza] Hi. How are you?

331
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:51,093
-[Both] Good to see you.
-[Patrick] How's it going?

332
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:53,470
Thanks for meeting me.
I really appreciate that.

333
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,432
-Okay. So I talked to my client.
-Uh-huh.

334
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:58,851
The house is great. Fits everything
about the L.A. lifestyle,

335
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,145
-everything we've been looking for.
-That's good.

336
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,272
But we looked at the comps,
days on market and such.

337
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:06,024
So, what he's come up with
and told me that I can offer is

338
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,152
two-two-seven-five, all cash.

339
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,571
-Okay.
-Seventeen-day inspection contingency.

340
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:11,989
[Both] Okay.

341
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:14,658
That's a start, let's see.
I'll make a call

342
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:17,536
-and I'll try to work some magic.
-Okay. Let me know, thank you.

343
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:20,372
I'm literally on the inside, like,

344
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:23,792
"Please buy this house.
I'll beg you. I'll pay you."

345
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:27,796
But I'm trying to keep it professional,
you know.

346
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,089
[phone rings]

347
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:32,051
-[man] Hello?
-Hi, it's Amanza. How are you?

348
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:34,887
-[man] I'm good. How are you?
-[Amanza] I'm doing well, thank you.

349
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:37,389
So we have an offer
on your Stanley listing.

350
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,183
It's an all-cash offer.

351
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:43,437
And they're coming in at two million,
two-hundred seventy-five thousand,

352
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:46,398
with a 17-day contingency.

353
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:51,236
[Alex] I know the amount I put 
into the remodel. I know what it's worth,

354
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:56,575
and I really can't take anything less
than $2,340,000.

355
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:58,035
And, if they're all cash,

356
00:17:58,118 --> 00:18:00,829
they can come in
with less of a contingency.

357
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:03,832
So if we could lower that to ten days,
then I think we can make a deal.

358
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,335
So $2,340,000

359
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:07,836
with a 10-day contingency

360
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,630
-and a 30-day close.
-[Alex] Okay.

361
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:11,548
I will see what he says.
I'll call you back.

362
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,550
-[Alex] Thank you, Amanza.
-Thank you, bye.

363
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:16,345
It's pretty normal for someone
to have a counteroffer.

364
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,931
I just hope that this price
is still in the range

365
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:21,016
that Patrick's client is willing to pay.

366
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,812
So, time to turn on the charm
and sell this house.

367
00:18:25,145 --> 00:18:29,149
[Amanza] Okay. So good news.
Now I know we can get this deal done.

368
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:32,236
But because of the upgrades,
all the renovations he's done,

369
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:35,155
comps in the area,
he's not comfortable with that offer.

370
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:39,034
He wants to come back with $2,340,000

371
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,453
and a 10-day contingency.

372
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:43,997
My buyer's in New York,

373
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:47,417
let me check, see what he thinks.
He's pretty quick usually, so…

374
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:50,921
[message typing]

375
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:53,382
-[Patrick groans]
-[laughs] The clock ticks.

376
00:18:54,174 --> 00:18:55,801
-[phone chimes]
-Oh, here he is.

377
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:00,639
[Patrick] Okay.

378
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:02,683
He'll take it.

379
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:05,978
I just sold a freaking house.
Should I do it?

380
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:11,233
Hallelujah, praise the Lord!

381
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,318
[bell clangs loudly]

382
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:15,571
That felt really good.

383
00:19:19,241 --> 00:19:21,660
[Patrick] You just made me very happy
because you have no idea

384
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:24,288
-how long it's taken me to buy it.
-And you just made me very happy

385
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:26,748
because this was
my first real estate sale.

386
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:27,791
-Shut up.
-[Amanza] Yes.

387
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,836
-I didn't know that.
-Yeah. I'm the newest agent at the office.

388
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:33,422
Oh, fantastic. Well, could've fooled me.

389
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:35,883
-Thank you. And he's a designer.
-Yes.

390
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:38,886
I sold, as a designer,
sold my first house to a designer.

391
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:41,972
-It was meant to be.
-There you go. We'll get things rolling,

392
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:44,725
put the contract out, we'll get it
taken care of and shoot it over…

393
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:46,435
-[Amanza] Yay!
-All good? Congratulations.

394
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:49,187
-I appreciate everything.
-[Amanza] Congratulations to you too.

395
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:50,105
I don't know how much

396
00:19:50,188 --> 00:19:52,649
their first sale means
to the other agents in the office,

397
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,569
but for me, it's so much more
than just the commission.

398
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:58,697
I'm doing it for my kids,
but I'm also doing it for myself.

399
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,992
I proved I'm not just a designer
or a stager,

400
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,203
I'm also a real estate agent now.

401
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,914
-[Patrick] Talk to you soon. Thanks.
-[Amanza] Have a good evening.

402
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:14,546
♪ Me, myself and I are making ♪

403
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:19,343
♪ Me, myself and I are making news ♪

404
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:21,762
♪ News… ♪

405
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,270
[Mary laughs]

406
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:33,106
-Oh!
-[Mary] I need some caffeine!

407
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:37,152
Christine, do you even know
how to do photocopies?

408
00:20:37,235 --> 00:20:39,571
[Christine] God, no.
I have people for that.

409
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:42,991
[Jason] I can't take Amanza seriously
in those glasses.

410
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:44,743
What? These are my glasses.

411
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,704
-[Heather] Let me see.
-[Maya] You look like a naughty teacher.

412
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:51,250
I'm going back to Miami next week.
I'm putting my penthouse

413
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,835
-back on the market.
-You are? That's awesome.

414
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:56,505
So I'm gonna spend some time there
for a while,

415
00:20:56,588 --> 00:20:58,924
and try to get some work you know, going.

416
00:20:59,007 --> 00:21:02,594
What is everyone doing for… New Year's?

417
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,096
I'm gonna be in the Bahamas.

418
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:05,180
[various] You are?

419
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,099
-Yeah.
-[Christine] How fun.

420
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:09,685
-You gotta go to Atlantis, just pop by.
-That's where we're going.

421
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:11,353
-You're staying there?
-[Maya] We are.

422
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:13,522
-Oh, that's so nice.
-We're staying there.

423
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:17,234
Heather and Amanza? 
Let me talk to you guys real quick.

424
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:18,485
Good luck.

425
00:21:18,986 --> 00:21:21,029
Oh, no. Is this good or bad?

426
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,031
[Amanza] Any time I've had to go
to Jason's desk,

427
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:25,617
-it's been bad news.
-[Jason] No, I've got you on the couch.

428
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,202
-Just sit up here.
-[Amanza] Okay.

429
00:21:27,285 --> 00:21:29,579
[Jason] You guys all know
the situation with Fennell

430
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:32,374
that I put them under,
where they were kind of under the gun.

431
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:34,084
And they had to use the concierge service

432
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:36,837
to fix up the entire house
and then get it sold immediately. 

433
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,839
They did exactly that.

434
00:21:39,881 --> 00:21:42,217
We got three offers in the first 48 hours.

435
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:43,593
[Christine] That's awesome.

436
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:45,303
[Jason] We were on the market
at 3.699.

437
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,764
-We're in escrow at 3.650.
-[Davina] Wow.

438
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:49,474
And we have two back-up offers behind it.

439
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:52,936
-So that house is sold. In 48 hours.
-[Mary] That's incredible. Nice.

440
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,063
I know. I know. She did good.

441
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,690
-Thank you.
-She did very, very good.

442
00:21:56,773 --> 00:22:00,736
Stanley, now Fennell too. I'm, like,
I can do it. I did it. I'm doing it.

443
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:01,903
I'll do it again.

444
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:04,197
I'm on a roll. [laughs]

445
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,825
-That's teamwork. Knew you would kill it.
-Good job.

446
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:07,951
Good job, guys.

447
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:11,163
When I first found out that I was working
with Amanza, I was like,

448
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:13,457
"Oof! This is gonna be very hard."

449
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:17,586
And now, seeing that we've pulled together
and how fast we pulled it together

450
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:19,755
and sold it very quickly,

451
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:23,258
I'm very proud of me and Amanza.
And I'd be happy to work with her again.

452
00:22:23,341 --> 00:22:24,384
Ring the bell!

453
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:26,261
-You ready?
-Ring the bell!

454
00:22:26,678 --> 00:22:29,514
Wait, hold on, I wanna video. I wanna
video. I wanna video. Hold on, hoes.

455
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:31,058
[Heather] Ready? And…

456
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:33,268
-Oh, wait!
-[Jason laughs]

457
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,519
Oh, my God.

458
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:38,190
[Heather] Go! No! Okay, you go.
-[Amanza] It's like tug-of-war.

459
00:22:38,273 --> 00:22:40,776
[bell clangs loudly]

460
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:42,694
-[Heather] Yay!
-[cheering, applause]

461
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,112
-We did it.
-I'm proud of you both.

462
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:46,823
Chrishell's not here for the bell.
She'd be so excited.

463
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:48,617
That was a good one. We did good.

464
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,161
["Brave" playing]
♪ This is my reason ♪

465
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:54,289
♪ It's why my heart's beating ♪

466
00:22:54,373 --> 00:22:56,750
♪ Just takes believing ♪

467
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:04,674
♪ I will be brave
Not gonna break ♪

468
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:07,594
♪ Don't care what they say… ♪

469
00:23:08,678 --> 00:23:09,513
[Shonda] Hey.

470
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:13,600
Oh, you guys already have the table.
I'll do the-- What else can I do to help?

471
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:17,687
We're gonna make a salad. And we're going
to probably pop the bread in the oven.

472
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,981
-[Chrishell] Yum.
-[Shonda] Where are the boys?

473
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:22,150
[Chrishell] Hey, bud.

474
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:23,068
Hey, Nicholas.

475
00:23:23,985 --> 00:23:25,278
-Dinner.
-[Nicholas] Okay.

476
00:23:25,362 --> 00:23:27,114
[Chrishell] You always do it up
with the food.

477
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:28,949
[Chrishell] Quality control.

478
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,035
Oh, my God. Those are so good.

479
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:32,953
[Chris] Ready?

480
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:36,581
[Chrishell] Oh, my God.
Chris, did you make all this food?

481
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:38,708
-[Chris] I had help.
-[Chrishell] Very impressive.

482
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:40,418
[Chris] Well, thank you. Wanna cut it?

483
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:44,965
Cutco knife,
I used to sell these door-to-door.

484
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:46,133
Did I sell you these?

485
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,968
-[Chris] Yes.
-[Shonda] Probably so.

486
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,929
-One of my first jobs.
-[Chris] One of your first sales.

487
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:53,849
[Savannah] I could not imagine you
as a door-to-door salesman.

488
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:57,811
Sold knives door-to-door.
How weird of a job was that?

489
00:23:57,894 --> 00:24:01,064
Like, "Hi, I have a bag of knives,
let me into your home."

490
00:24:01,148 --> 00:24:03,525
[Savannah] Yeah, that's fun.
You worked your way up.

491
00:24:03,608 --> 00:24:04,609
I worked my way up.

492
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:07,446
[Savannah] Now you sell multimillion
dollar mansions, and that's great.

493
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:08,905
-Yes.
-Anything is possible.

494
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:12,617
Well, yeah. It could be worse,
getting kicked out of my home. [laughs]

495
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:15,495
I could be selling knives door-to-door,
guys. [laughs]

496
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:18,790
My sister, Shonda, has been married
to Chris for almost 20 years now.

497
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:22,419
They have three kids,
which are all teenagers at this point.

498
00:24:22,502 --> 00:24:23,628
[Chris] Dig in, guys.

499
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:28,925
[Chrishell] And I'm crashing.
So they have their hands full.

500
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:33,430
I haven't had much of an appetite lately,
I will say, this is like,

501
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:35,640
this will do it. This looks so good.

502
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:39,019
Sometimes in L.A.,
we get too caught up in things

503
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:41,688
that are supposed to matter
that really don't.

504
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:43,607
And being here, you know,

505
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:47,736
this is-- this is exactly
what I think really does matter

506
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:50,322
and really is something to be so proud of.

507
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:53,200
They've been married so long,
and they have this beautiful family,

508
00:24:53,283 --> 00:24:56,077
and I just think
it's really hard to be around

509
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:57,412
because that's what I wanted,

510
00:24:57,495 --> 00:24:59,789
and that's what
I'm realizing I don't have.

511
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:02,876
But it helps me be inspired

512
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:05,629
to know that it might be out there.

513
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:09,466
It just might take a different path
than what I was thinking.

514
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:11,259
So what are you guys up to?

515
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:14,554
[Savannah] I just started taking
my GED classes again.

516
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:15,847
Nice.

517
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:18,183
I really want my GED
so I can apprentice with Mom.

518
00:25:18,266 --> 00:25:20,268
-[Chris] Yes.
-Is that what you're planning on doing?

519
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:23,605
-Yes, we're working on a five-year plan.
-I love that.

520
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:27,484
-[Chris] That's what we're doing.
-That's exciting. And I know you built

521
00:25:27,567 --> 00:25:29,194
your own game console?

522
00:25:29,653 --> 00:25:30,737
[Nicholas] Gaming PC.

523
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:32,822
-That's amazing.
-[Shonda] It's a whole computer.

524
00:25:32,906 --> 00:25:35,075
I feel like I've been coming
from a situation where

525
00:25:35,158 --> 00:25:38,286
all the focus is on me,
and all the questions are directed my way,

526
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,539
and it feels almost like an interrogation.

527
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:43,708
And so it is nice to talk
about other people, you know?

528
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:45,293
It's nice to be able to ask,

529
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:47,504
"What about this?
And what about your school?"

530
00:25:47,587 --> 00:25:51,049
You can kind of, for a second,
feel like everything's normal.

531
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:52,592
Have you sold any, like,

532
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,928
really big houses lately? Like, expensive?

533
00:25:55,011 --> 00:26:00,183
I did actually,
just sold over four million in the Valley.

534
00:26:00,267 --> 00:26:02,143
So, that was a big sale.

535
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:04,980
Well, I had a really good lead,
but I had to…

536
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:09,609
I had to hand it over just because I had
to leave town, but that's okay.

537
00:26:09,693 --> 00:26:10,902
So how are the girls?

538
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,738
Christine is getting married
when I get back.

539
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:14,864
[Shonda gasps]

540
00:26:14,948 --> 00:26:17,325
So her and I are on good terms
and everything,

541
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:22,330
but a wedding is on another level.
I haven't decided if I'm gonna go or not.

542
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:25,125
I don't want to be
at someone's wedding crying.

543
00:26:25,583 --> 00:26:26,751
I just don't know.

544
00:26:27,502 --> 00:26:28,795
I have to think about it.

545
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:32,424
I have a lot of anxiety
when I think about going back to L.A.

546
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:34,884
I just don't know that I want to.

547
00:26:35,343 --> 00:26:39,431
Now I feel like, okay, like,
I have a lot to get done, and…

548
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:40,974
let me, like…

549
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:44,853
get my… wind underneath me

550
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:46,187
and kinda, you know…

551
00:26:46,688 --> 00:26:49,566
You're one of the strongest people I know.
You can get through anything,

552
00:26:49,649 --> 00:26:53,194
-just keep your head up. You'll be fine.
-Thank you.

553
00:26:53,820 --> 00:26:55,238
You're so sweet. Thank you.

554
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,132
So I'll see him at the gym five times--

555
00:27:14,215 --> 00:27:15,425
Brett, just relax.

556
00:27:15,842 --> 00:27:16,968
[Heather] Hi.

557
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:20,221
-Hey. How are you?
-I'll sit by a heat lamp. Can I?

558
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,849
-[Davina] I like this place.
-I've been a couple of times.

559
00:27:22,932 --> 00:27:24,601
[Heather] You guys realize this is vegan?

560
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:26,853
-Yes. I'm excited to try it.
-Did you pick this spot?

561
00:27:26,936 --> 00:27:29,397
[Heather] Did I give a suggestion?
-I thought you picked it--

562
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:30,440
-Okay, I picked it.

563
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:33,109
At the Oppenheim Group,
we have a great balance,

564
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:36,404
we work very hard,
but we also celebrate our wins,

565
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:38,114
and I'm really proud of all the girls.

566
00:27:38,198 --> 00:27:39,658
Hello, ladies.

567
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:40,867
-Hey.
-[Jason] Hi, ladies.

568
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:44,412
Jason and Brett, that's a given.
But I'm really proud of all my girls.

569
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,331
We're doing a kick-ass job this year.

570
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:49,042
Nice, perfect.
I'm ready for some chips and wine.

571
00:27:49,125 --> 00:27:50,377
[Davina] I'm starving.

572
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:52,003
-[Maya] Amanza's coming, right?
-Yeah.

573
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:53,588
-Yeah she is.
-[Brett] She better.

574
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:55,256
-[Maya] Cool.
-[Jason] That looks good.

575
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,549
[Heather] We can't eat that.

576
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:59,302
-Hello.
-Hi.

577
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:00,970
-Where should I sit?
-[Mary] Hey, girl.

578
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:02,389
Wherever, here, here.

579
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:04,307
[Maya] Hey, Amanza. Hi.

580
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:06,267
Is Christine coming?
Do you know where she is?

581
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:08,144
[Maya] Christine's dog got lost, I think…

582
00:28:08,228 --> 00:28:10,188
-No way.
-…so I think she's looking for him.

583
00:28:10,271 --> 00:28:11,481
Can you pass the cauliflower?

584
00:28:11,564 --> 00:28:14,609
-[Davina] The salad looks good.
-[Maya] I love it. Salad.

585
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:17,404
Guys, I'm glad we all got together
'cause there's a lot to celebrate.

586
00:28:17,487 --> 00:28:19,572
Amanza, Heather,
you guys just crushed it on Fennell.

587
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:22,075
We have the concierge service
moving forward.

588
00:28:22,158 --> 00:28:24,035
Amanza also took care of Stanley recently.

589
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:25,495
You're killing it.

590
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:26,621
Mary impressed her client,

591
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:28,957
he is giving us an eight
and a 12 million dollar listing.

592
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,875
-[Heather] Wow.
-Star associate, right here.

593
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,378
-[Amanza] Sold her wedding venue that day.
-[Jason] Unbiasedly.

594
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:34,879
[Davina] That's totally unbiased.

595
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:37,340
With the Hillside sale,
we'll be getting larger listings.

596
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:39,426
-Amazing.
-[Jason] We're in nine escrows.

597
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:42,345
As a brokerage,
we're 18 percent this year over last year.

598
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:44,764
This has been an amazing year.
I'm proud of everyone.

599
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:45,890
-Cheers.
-Good job, guys.

600
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,852
[all] Good job. Congrats. Cheers!

601
00:28:49,769 --> 00:28:51,813
-[Heather] Cheers to us.
-[Jason] Onwards and upwards.

602
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:54,190
-This is only the beginning.
-[Maya] L.A. is a great market,

603
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:57,110
but I have a lot of big changes
coming in my life.

604
00:28:57,193 --> 00:29:01,781
And it makes me think a lot
in what I'm actually going to do.

605
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:04,325
Should I focus in Miami real estate?

606
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:06,411
Should I just leave the Oppenheim Group?

607
00:29:06,494 --> 00:29:08,580
I don't know. I have a lot to think about.

608
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:11,416
-[Maya] As I opened the diaper--
-[Jason] Hey, honey.

609
00:29:11,499 --> 00:29:13,585
-[Davina] Oh, really?
-[Amanza] There she is.

610
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:15,587
-Hey.
-Sit here, sweetheart. Sit here.

611
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:18,423
-[Mary] You look so cute.
-[Amanza] She made it.

612
00:29:18,506 --> 00:29:20,467
-[Davina] I love her purse.
-[Mary] You found him.

613
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:23,595
Teddy ran away
like the Harry Houdini that he is,

614
00:29:23,678 --> 00:29:26,055
and I am looking for him for hours.

615
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:29,434
I finally found him, and I'm so stressed.

616
00:29:30,018 --> 00:29:32,353
If I lost Teddy,
I don't think I could live.

617
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:34,355
I could get another husband
but not another dog.

618
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:36,149
Went on every single door.

619
00:29:36,232 --> 00:29:39,110
-[Maya] Did you ask if they'd sell?
-Christine finally went door knocking.

620
00:29:39,194 --> 00:29:40,820
[all laughing] Yeah!

621
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:43,698
-Wait, where's Chrishell?
-She, um…

622
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:45,867
…she's staying in St. Louis
for a little while longer.

623
00:29:45,950 --> 00:29:49,204
You guys really believe that she was,
like, blindsided by this?

624
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:52,999
A thousand percent!
I think she was blindsided.

625
00:29:53,082 --> 00:29:54,751
You think they had problems
for a while?

626
00:29:54,834 --> 00:29:57,587
I mean, every relationship has,
like, small problems.

627
00:29:57,670 --> 00:30:00,089
I mean, you always have small arguments,
you have--

628
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,801
And I don't even know the details
about anything, but it was nothing.

629
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:05,220
She was one hundred percent blindsided.

630
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:07,805
[Davina] Mary and Amanza are
die-hard Chrishell, and that's fine.

631
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:11,267
And I would love to support Chrishell,
but I have met Justin before.

632
00:30:11,351 --> 00:30:15,313
Justin was nothing but a gentleman to me,
he was very warm and kind and polite.

633
00:30:15,396 --> 00:30:20,235
So whether you didn't expect them
to necessarily file for divorce that day,

634
00:30:20,318 --> 00:30:22,821
fair enough,
you can say you didn't expect that,

635
00:30:22,904 --> 00:30:24,030
and that's believable.

636
00:30:24,113 --> 00:30:26,866
But you knew
things were probably not going well.

637
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:30,495
[Amanza] She feels humiliated,
which she shouldn't.

638
00:30:30,578 --> 00:30:32,163
-No, she shouldn't.
-[Amanza] If anybody--

639
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:33,998
-She was the best. From what I--
-…it's him.

640
00:30:34,082 --> 00:30:36,584
-[Maya] Why would she feel humiliated?
-Like, it's out there.

641
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:38,795
Like, your husband divorced you,
that's embarrassing.

642
00:30:38,878 --> 00:30:43,258
And everyone's writing her and messaging
and social media and it's, like--

643
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:44,676
It should be embarrassing for him.

644
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:47,220
I feel like Justin was a very,
like, solid, steady--

645
00:30:47,303 --> 00:30:49,472
-[Amanza] We don't know.
-…predictable. We don't know,

646
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:51,432
-you're right.
-[Amanza] You met at a party.

647
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:54,185
Even when Chrishell
wasn't talking to me and Davina,

648
00:30:54,269 --> 00:30:57,397
he was really nice, and,
like, he went out of his way to, like--

649
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:59,649
Even though Chrishell was like,
"No, don't talk to them."

650
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:02,819
He went out of his way
to come over to us and say,

651
00:31:02,902 --> 00:31:03,903
"Hey, so good to see you."

652
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:06,781
Like, you know? Like, he was, like,
really nice and warm and polite,

653
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:07,866
endearing and--

654
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:09,826
That doesn't feel
like a very supportive husband.

655
00:31:09,909 --> 00:31:12,620
So maybe you can look at it like,
"Oh, he's super sweet."

656
00:31:12,704 --> 00:31:14,622
[Davina] It's what we do know of him
was positive.

657
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:16,332
Just saying that he was very positive.

658
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:20,378
If I ask my man not to speak to somebody
because I'm having issues with them,

659
00:31:21,170 --> 00:31:23,298
and he goes out of his way
to talk to them.

660
00:31:23,381 --> 00:31:26,217
That's not a good partner.
Like, that's an ass.

661
00:31:26,301 --> 00:31:30,179
And even if you thought that was nice,
keep it to your fucking self.

662
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:32,348
We're not talking good
about him. There's nothing good

663
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:33,891
that he can do. Nothing.

664
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:35,935
There is no Justin.

665
00:31:36,352 --> 00:31:38,313
I just think
there's two sides to every story,

666
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:40,565
and maybe
they've been having problems for a while.

667
00:31:40,648 --> 00:31:43,026
And she just didn't think
it was gonna come down to this,

668
00:31:43,109 --> 00:31:45,737
and he had enough. You just never know
what really happened.

669
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:47,697
[Davina] He has to have
a side of the story.

670
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:51,784
[Mary] Davina's never even met Justin,
so I don't know why she's

671
00:31:51,868 --> 00:31:53,119
even getting involved.

672
00:31:53,202 --> 00:31:57,165
[Amanza] Well, she's our friend,
so the judgment call is Team Chrishell.

673
00:31:57,248 --> 00:31:59,375
-Oh, yeah. There's no question.
-[Amanza] Period.

674
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,294
We don't need to know what his side is.

675
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:04,088
In my opinion, there's not two sides.

676
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:07,008
The right side is Chrishell's side,
because she is our family.

677
00:32:07,091 --> 00:32:08,885
And we support her. Period.

678
00:32:08,968 --> 00:32:10,762
["Fearless" playing]

679
00:32:11,804 --> 00:32:13,598
♪ That's what they say ♪

680
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:19,562
♪ Though you find it hard to make a play ♪

681
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:22,065
♪ You've been hurt before ♪

682
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:25,777
♪ And you're keeping score ♪

683
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:27,946
♪ So you never give yourself… ♪

684
00:32:28,404 --> 00:32:29,405
[Chrishell] Alright.

685
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:34,619
[Shonda] I am so glad you got to visit.

686
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:40,166
[Shonda] Don't forget, we're always here.
You can come any time.

687
00:32:40,249 --> 00:32:42,627
You go back, you make your house a home.

688
00:32:42,710 --> 00:32:45,880
Remember where we came from.
You've lived in a car.

689
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:48,383
This is nothing. You got this.

690
00:32:48,466 --> 00:32:49,300
Thank you.

691
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:50,968
I just love you so much.

692
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:52,595
Love you too.

693
00:32:52,679 --> 00:32:57,141
♪ No matter the stars
You know who you are ♪

694
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:58,976
-[Chrishell] Thank you.
-[Shonda] I love you.

695
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:00,144
[Chrishell] Love you too.

696
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:01,980
-I got this.
-[Shonda] You got this.

697
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:04,023
Right? Thank you.

698
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:06,025
Bye! Have a safe trip. I love you!

699
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:07,819
[Shonda] Bye!

700
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:12,365
♪ We're fearless ♪

701
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:16,661
♪ Fearless ♪

702
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:20,248
[Chrishell] This is not something
that I ever wanted for myself,

703
00:33:20,331 --> 00:33:22,375
but I have been through a lot
in my life,

704
00:33:22,458 --> 00:33:24,961
so I know that I have a strength
inside of me.

705
00:33:25,294 --> 00:33:27,338
I know that I will get through this.

706
00:33:27,422 --> 00:33:29,549
♪ You know who you are ♪

707
00:33:30,758 --> 00:33:37,348
♪ Your spirit is fearless… ♪

708
00:33:48,943 --> 00:33:51,154
♪ Fearless ♪

709
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:55,241
♪ Fearless ♪

